// The building is a six-storey reinforced concrete residential structure comprising 48 dwelling units distributed across five upper floors above a ground-level common area and parking level. The building footprint is approximately 40 m × 18 m, oriented along an east-west axis.
// The ground floor accommodates a lobby and reception area, a central mail room, two elevators, an enclosed stairwell at each end of the building, a bicycle storage room, building services and plant rooms (including electrical switchboard, water metering, and telecommunications), and an enclosed parking garage with 52 spaces accessed via a ramp from the northern facade.
// Floors one through five each contain eight to ten apartments arranged along a central corridor. The unit mix includes studio apartments (approximately 35 m²), one-bedroom units (approximately 55 m²), two-bedroom units (approximately 75 m²), and a smaller number of three-bedroom corner units (approximately 95 m²). Each unit includes an open-plan kitchen and living area, a separate bathroom with shower, and private balconies ranging from 6 to 12 m² accessible from the living area.
// The structural system consists of a flat slab concrete frame with shear walls at the elevator and stair cores providing lateral stability. External walls are clad with an insulated rendered facade system. The roof is a flat roof with a bituminous membrane waterproofing layer, incorporating drainage to internal downpipes. A communal rooftop terrace occupies approximately one third of the roof area.
// Shared facilities include a laundry room on the ground floor, a waste management room with separated recycling streams, and landscaped communal outdoor space to the south of the building. The building is served by a central hot water system, individual heat pump units per dwelling for heating and cooling, mechanical ventilation with heat recovery in all units, and a fire sprinkler system throughout.
// The building is designed to comply with applicable accessibility requirements, with step-free access to all common areas and a minimum of 10% of units designed as fully accessible dwellings.

// Six-storey reinforced concrete residential building
// 48 dwelling units across 5 upper floors + ground-level common areas and parking
// Footprint: 40m x 18m, oriented east-west
//
// Layout key:
//   x-axis: 0 (west) to 40 (east)
//   y-axis: 0 (south, main entrance) to 18 (north, parking ramp)
//   Central corridor: y=8 to y=10 on residential floors
//   West stair core: x=0 to x=3
//   East stair core: x=37 to x=40
//   Elevator core: x=19 to x=21

